# things were wrong with it: the URL is 404, because Raspberry Pi
# removes old images from downloads.raspberrypi.com, and the dev board
# was never running it. `/etc/rpi-issue` on the board says "Raspberry Pi
# reference 2026-06-18", Debian 13 trixie, built by pi-gen at commit
# ca8aeed0ae300c2a89f55ce9617d5f96a27e99e5, stage2. That is this image.
#
# THE HASH BELOW WAS COMPUTED HERE, not copied. The whole 524,875,608
# bytes were downloaded on 2026-09-23 and hashed, and the result matched
# the .sha256 the Foundation publishes beside the file.
#
# It is a weaker pin than CORE_SHA256 and the difference is worth
# knowing. Core's hash is attested by eleven GPG signatures from keys
# served by a different host. This one has no signature at all: the
# image and its hash come from the same server, so it proves you got
# what we got and proves nothing about what that is. Raspberry Pi OS
# images are also not reproducible by anyone, the Foundation included,
# so nobody can rebuild this file and compare. The pi-gen commit above
# is the nearest thing to a recipe.
